<title>NETHERLANDS: HEIJMANS H1 NET PROFIT FLAT.</title>
<headline>HEIJMANS H1 NET PROFIT FLAT.</headline>
<dateline>ROSMALEN, Netherlands 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>H1 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     3.70 vs   3.85</p>
<p>    Net profit			    12.5  vs  same</p>
<p>    Turnover			     569    vs 576</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			20.0  vs  20.0</p>
<p>    Cash flow			     28.1  vs  25.5</p>
<p>    Order book (billions)		1.06 vs   1.04</p>
<p>NOTES - Construction firm Heijmans NV said the temporary</p>
<p>slowdown in growth of revenues and profits was caused by a long</p>
<p>period of very cold weather at the beginning of the year.</p>
<p>First-half results include contribution to revenues and</p>
<p>profits of newly acquired units, De Enk, Van Helvoirt, Vos en</p>
<p>Teeuwissen and increased stakes in Belgian units BAB and ACA.</p>
<p>Number of shares in issue rose 3.6 percent to 3.38 million.</p>
<p>Order book figure states value of orders at end of period.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
